IEEE International Conference on Cluster Computing
September 8-11, 2015
Chicago, IL, USA
http://www.mcs.anl.gov/ieeecluster2015/

**** NEWS ****

  * 38 full papers accepted out of 157 submissions (24% acceptance rate)
  * 28 short papers with oral presentations
  * 30 peer-reviewed posters
  * 3 keynotes
  * 6 workshops
  * Panel on exascale computing
  * 2 industry sessions with talks from Cray and DDN
  * Student Mentoring Program
  * Student Travel Support
  * Early bird registration: July 25th, 2015
  * Hotel Reservation: August 17th, 2015


**** CALL FOR PARTICIPATION ****
Clusters have become the workhorse for computational science and=20
engineering research, powering innovation and discovery that advance=20
science and society. They are the base for building today=E2=80=99s rapid=
ly=20
evolving cloud and HPC infrastructures, and are used to solve some of=20
the most complex problems. Clusters are the base for building today=E2=80=
=99s=20
rapidly evolving cloud and HPC infrastructure, and are used to solve=20
some of the most complex problems. The challenge to make them scalable,=20
efficient, and more functional requires the common effort of the cluster=20
community in the areas of cluster system design, management and=20
monitoring =E2=80=94 at hardware, system, middleware, and application lev=
el. The=20
IEEE Cluster conference has precisely this goal: to be a major venue for=20
such collective effort.

We are happy to announce a rich, high-quality conference program for=20
IEEE Cluster 2015 with 38 full papers accepted out of 157 submissions=20
that went through a selective reviewing process (over 600 reviews),=20
resulting in an acceptance rate of 24%. In addition the conference=20
features 28 short papers and 30 peer-reviewed posters present exciting,=20
emergent research directions.

The conference program includes three keynotes, six workshops, a panel=20
on exascale computing, and two industry sessions with talks from Cray=20
and Data Direct Networks (DDN) - two major players with high impact in=20
the area of cluster computing. We continue the successful Student=20
Mentoring Program specific to PhD students, which will include student=20
travel support; for more information, see=20
http://www.mcs.anl.gov/ieeecluster2015/student-program/.

The entire program of IEEE Cluster is now available at=20
http://press3.mcs.anl.gov/ieeecluster2015/conference-program/technical-pr=
ogram.

The Organizing Committee is happy to welcome you to Chicago and hopes=20
you find Cluster 2015 an exciting and intellectually stimulating event!

*Venue and Accommodation*
The conference and the affiliated workshops are held in the Double Tree=20
Hotel Chicago Magnificent Mile, which is centrally located and within=20
walking distance of numerous attractions in downtown Chicago, Illinois.=20
The hotel is holding a block of rooms reserved at a very special rate=20
for Cluster 2015 participants.

Book your room at:=20
http://www.mcs.anl.gov/ieeecluster2015/registration-and-accommodation/acc=
ommodation/

*Registration*
Register for the conference at=20
http://www.mcs.anl.gov/ieeecluster2015/registration-and-accommodation/reg=
istration/
*
**Important Dates*
Early Bird Conference Registration Cut-off Date: July 25, 2015
Hotel Reservation Cut-off: August 17, 2015
Main Conference: September  8-11, 2015
Workshops: September 8, 2015

